# Copy to .env for local development:  cp .env.example .env
#
# These are read by the server-side functions only (netlify/functions/*.mjs).
# None are prefixed with VITE_, so Vite will never include them in the browser
# bundle. Do not add a VITE_ prefix to any of them — that would publish them.
#
# On Netlify, set the same variables under:
#   Site configuration -> Environment variables

# --- Anthropic, for the career match, resume and interview features ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- AutoTrain Decision Tree, for the strand classifier ---

# OPTIONAL. The prediction endpoint is compiled into classify.mjs, taken from
# the Testing Console's own request:
#
#   https://api.autotrain.app/api/autotrain/jobs/<job id>/predict?access=dashboard
#
# Prediction is per training job, so retraining issues a new job id and the
# compiled-in URL goes stale — that shows up as a 404. When it does, copy the
# fresh Request URL out of the Testing Console's Network tab and set it here.
# AUTOTRAIN_URL=

# --- Authentication (REQUIRED) ---
# The endpoint answers "401 Dashboard authentication is required" without a
# bearer token. Pick ONE of the two routes below. Either way the token is read
# here, server-side, and never reaches the browser.
#
# ROUTE A — the credential itself. Copy the Authorization header value from
# the Testing Console's successful request; pasting the whole thing including
# the leading "Bearer " is fine, it is stripped.
#
# Note the lifetime: if that header holds a Firebase ID token (it starts
# "eyJ" and is very long), it stops working ONE HOUR after it was issued, and
# the site answers 401 again until the value is replaced. Good for confirming
# everything else works; see Route B to stop re-pasting it.
# AUTOTRAIN_API_KEY=

# ROUTE B — let the function mint its own. Keeps working indefinitely: a
# refresh token does not expire unless revoked, and the function exchanges it
# for a fresh ID token whenever the cached one is within five minutes of
# running out. Both values are needed.
#
#   AUTOTRAIN_REFRESH_TOKEN     in the Testing Console, DevTools ->
#                               Application -> IndexedDB -> firebaseLocalStorage
#                               -> your user record -> stsTokenManager
#                               -> refreshToken
#   AUTOTRAIN_FIREBASE_API_KEY  the project's web API key. In the same
#                               DevTools Network tab, any request to
#                               identitytoolkit.googleapis.com or
#                               securetoken.googleapis.com carries it as ?key=
#                               Either spelling works: AUTOTRAIN_FIREBASE_API_KEY
#                               or AUTOTRAIN_FIREBASE_APIKEY. Setting one half
#                               of the pair without the other is reported
#                               rather than ignored.
# AUTOTRAIN_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# AUTOTRAIN_FIREBASE_API_KEY=

# Treat both routes as secrets: they authenticate as your AutoTrain account.
# .env is git-ignored; on Netlify they live in the site's environment.
